  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Climate Resilience and  Food Security Enhancement Initiative (CRFSEI) Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The area of Sutarkhali Union is 50 square kilometres known as the climate vulnerable zone. The union is 
located on the south west of Bangladesh which exposes it to constant climate hazards such as 
cyclones, tidal surges, riverbank erosion, salinity intrusion and more. Salinity intrusion particularly affects the 
community as there is crop production damage leading to unstable livelihoods and scarcity 
of drinking water. People residing in the union are suffering every year from cyclones and heavy rainfall. 
Saline water enters into farming lands and limits farmers ability to cultivate their lands.
Through the project initiatives, the vulnerable women will be united through establishing self-help groups (SHG) and be trained on different development issues for adopting climate change mitigation and reduction 
of disaster risks through project implementation. At the same time, through SHG formation, they will aware 
on women rights, participate in different events like conflict resolution, gender and development, accumulate 
savings for future development and thus they will be empowered in their villages, communities and lead other 
women to engage with local government bodies. By organizing selected families into community 
organizations (Self Help Groups) to address to their needs as poor and 
marginalized they can collectively address their social and economic needs and are able to respond 
to Climate Change Adaptations and Mitigations (CCAM) and Reduce Disaster Risks (DRR) in the most 
appropriate way.</narrative>
  </description>
